Z||000000||RedHaze86SD4||11-19-2001||11:56 AM||||Just thought I'd tell everyone about my current project. I'm redoing the interior on my 86 SC to all black.. It was dark and medium grey. I've already got both doors retrimmed with black immitation leather where the carpeting was. the console under the shifter plate is also recovered. next up is the dash and the headliner. The carpeting is being redone with black also, but will have to wait till next payday for that part. What do you think? Factory style carpet or something longer and softer? I'm thinking factory style... Anyways, I'll post final pictures when I get through. If anyone wants to know more just ask.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>The Possabilities are only hindered by your imagination and will to make them come alive....<P>-=Red Haze.. Its coming=-||||reg||1
Z||000001||falconhulk||11-19-2001||12:06 PM||||Going to do the same thing this spring.   Think I am going to have my upolster do it though as he is real good and pretty cheap.  Only charged me 400 to redo and recover my doors, dash, and console in  my mustang.  How long did it take you to pull everything out to dye it?  Seems like a whole lot of work.<p>[This message has been edited by falconhulk (edited 11-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||RedHaze86SD4||11-19-2001||12:17 PM||||The doors were kinda hard. I'm starting in on the rest of the console now and the dash overlay next. The doors took me 4 hours. the hard part was pulling the carpet and cleaning the factory glue. Its a PAIN. But the end result looks factory. I opted for padding under the im-leather though so its a little "puffy" looking, nt much and the al black looks -=sweet=- As for the dye scratching... I tryed to scratch up a spare peice before I started, and as long as you let it set good and coat it enough, it doesnt scratch easily...<P>------------------<BR>The Possabilities are only hindered by your imagination and will to make them come alive....<P>-=Red Haze.. Its coming=-||||reg||1
